name yardstick_390_rtcp_clock_1
describe issue_204_cross_traffic_join with libwebrtc's clock starting at 107919 s, so its RTCPSender draws another RTCP schedule: does libwebrtc stick above capacity on any of 80 seeds under it (yardstick for #390)
# libwebrtc on its default clock (100000 s): 0 of 80 seeds stuck (>= 10 freezes), #389. Ours: 3 of 80 on main's schedule,
# 5 of 80 under a schedule drawn as libwebrtc's. Our side is unchanged by this key.
compare_seeds 80
compare_clock_start 107919
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=40ms queue=300ms
at 10s cross=2000kbps
at 25s cross=0kbps
